# Vercel auto-deploy — Michael Hart Consulting Website

This rule applies **only** to **Michael Hart Consulting Website** (`MH_Consulting_Website`), which deploys to Vercel from `main`. **Do not** auto-push any other repository.

After completing any substantive change here (especially under `website/`), **commit and push to `main`** to trigger the Vercel deployment. Do not wait for the user to ask.

## Workflow

1. Finish the requested code change and verify the build when practical (`npm run build` in `website/`).
2. Stage only files related to the task — never `.env`, secrets, or unrelated local edits.
3. Commit with a clear message focused on why the change was made.
4. Push to `origin main` unless the user specifies a different branch.

## Git safety (still applies)

- Never update git config, force-push to `main`, or skip hooks unless explicitly requested.
- Never commit secrets (`.env`, credentials, API keys).
- If push is blocked or requires approval, retry with approval after explaining what will be deployed.

## Other projects

For any repo that is **not** this Vercel site, follow the default rule: **only commit or push when the user asks**. Other projects are not on Vercel yet.

## Scope

This overrides “only commit when asked” **for this repository only**. Question-only or review-only tasks with no file changes do not require a commit or push.
